WEBVTT

00:06.006 --> 00:07.799
Was there a Vaccine card?

00:07.882 --> 00:09.676
No. It was all for nothing.

00:10.468 --> 00:11.886
What do we do now?

00:21.229 --> 00:22.397
What's wrong?

00:23.106 --> 00:24.315
You don't look so good.

00:26.026 --> 00:28.945
- I… I'm fine.
- No lying, now.

00:30.447 --> 00:33.450
Be honest.
Did someone turn you into a zombie?

00:36.953 --> 00:39.289
I… Yeah. I was infected.

00:39.372 --> 00:42.417
- He was trying to hide it!
- No! I was just about to tell you.

00:42.500 --> 00:44.919
And besides, I remember
the face of the guy who did this to me.

00:47.213 --> 00:48.673
Then let's fucking kill him.

00:50.633 --> 00:52.385
You. You're up next.

00:53.678 --> 00:56.264
- Go kill that zombie.
- Me?

00:58.349 --> 01:00.060
No. Send someone else.

01:00.769 --> 01:02.771
This one's practically still a kid.

01:03.438 --> 01:05.982
It's okay. Pick someone else.

01:06.066 --> 01:10.236
Bro, how is that fair for the people who
already had to use their Shotgun cards?

01:12.572 --> 01:16.076
What, you think anybody here
actually wants to take a life, huh?

01:17.619 --> 01:19.788
No one should be forced to kill anyone.

01:24.375 --> 01:26.336
You think you're better than us? Hmm?

01:26.419 --> 01:29.714
I bet you've killed someone
in a game before.

01:37.931 --> 01:41.059
Surviving these games is impossible
without some sacrifice.

01:45.688 --> 01:46.689
Go on.

01:48.900 --> 01:50.026
No. Stay!

01:50.110 --> 01:51.111
Arisu!

01:51.194 --> 01:53.196
- What the hell?
- Hold him down!

01:55.198 --> 01:56.825
Now, if you don't go,

01:58.576 --> 02:00.286
we'll shoot this guy instead.

02:03.915 --> 02:06.292
Don't… do it.

02:06.376 --> 02:10.547
Please, Ikeno.
There's gotta be another way.

02:19.389 --> 02:21.099
Show your cards.

02:36.990 --> 02:38.158
I'm sorry.

04:07.163 --> 04:08.623
I'm so sorry.

04:23.179 --> 04:25.014
Four rounds remain.

04:25.098 --> 04:28.434
Please choose your opponent
and touch them.

04:46.452 --> 04:48.246
You took your sweet time.

04:51.708 --> 04:52.709
Yeah.

04:53.710 --> 04:55.211
Did you do it?

05:00.842 --> 05:02.302
Yeah, it's done.

05:10.268 --> 05:12.687
Good job, kid. Yeah!

05:14.772 --> 05:16.607
Clap for him. Clap!

05:18.735 --> 05:19.944
Ah-he-hem!

05:20.028 --> 05:22.113
Way to go!

05:44.802 --> 05:46.054
Where's Nobu?

05:46.137 --> 05:48.306
Oh, he said he was coming right back.

06:11.245 --> 06:12.288
Nobu?

06:18.669 --> 06:20.380
- Stop!
- Hey.

06:20.463 --> 06:22.090
Let go of me!

06:28.179 --> 06:31.099
This guy…
he turned that kid into a zombie.

06:31.641 --> 06:32.517
What kid?

06:34.769 --> 06:37.105
- Nobu's a zombie now?
- Yeah, that's right.

06:37.188 --> 06:38.606
Not Nobu…

06:40.191 --> 06:41.901
Well, where did he go?

06:42.402 --> 06:45.238
I saw him! He went off that way, alone.

06:46.030 --> 06:48.032
That son of a bitch.

06:49.492 --> 06:50.493
Bring him back!

06:50.576 --> 06:52.537
- Got it!
- Let's go!

06:53.454 --> 06:56.332
The zombies are trying
to hide their infections.

06:56.916 --> 07:00.211
Like Masato did. Nobu too, same thing.

07:00.294 --> 07:02.672
Maybe there's even more zombies among us…

07:05.258 --> 07:06.634
Yeah, you're right.

07:07.260 --> 07:10.012
Some of you are suspicious.

07:21.441 --> 07:23.526
N… no.

07:23.609 --> 07:24.986
No! I'm not, no!

07:25.069 --> 07:27.363
Wait, hang on! He's just…

07:27.864 --> 07:29.740
It's symptoms of drug withdrawal.

07:30.616 --> 07:33.953
Boss, what about the girl
who started all this? She's a zombie.

07:35.496 --> 07:38.541
Come to think of it… where did she get to?

07:39.667 --> 07:41.043
What if she's…

07:41.544 --> 07:44.172
Maybe the zombies have been spying on us.

07:45.131 --> 07:46.299
What?

07:46.382 --> 07:50.011
Well, do we even know
if she has a Vaccine card?

07:50.094 --> 07:52.180
What if it was all a lie?

07:53.347 --> 07:57.310
Yeah, what if her plan was to infect
a bunch of us the whole time she was here?

07:57.393 --> 07:58.478
Huh?

08:07.278 --> 08:10.072
The game's almost over now, anyway.

08:13.409 --> 08:15.995
I don't think we need the zombies
in order to win.

08:16.621 --> 08:18.998
If you find a zombie in here,
just shoot 'em.

08:39.852 --> 08:41.020
Sh!

08:42.605 --> 08:44.982
What are you doing?

08:45.066 --> 08:46.734
- What?
- Come on, let's go.

08:46.817 --> 08:49.153
- They're not going to…
- No…

08:51.656 --> 08:53.574
- Let's go.
- You're hurting me!

08:57.578 --> 09:00.206
- He's getting away!
- Stop! Someone get him!

09:17.181 --> 09:18.224
Hey!

09:20.351 --> 09:23.187
Just a sec.
Uh, I need you to do me a favor.

09:23.896 --> 09:25.106
What favor?

09:25.189 --> 09:27.817
Can… can you… use your vaccine on me?

09:28.484 --> 09:30.361
He's here!

09:32.863 --> 09:35.241
- No. No, please, don't! Don't kill me!
- Stop running!

09:35.324 --> 09:36.617
Don't! Get away from me!

09:37.410 --> 09:38.536
Get up.

09:38.619 --> 09:40.705
Three rounds remain.

09:40.788 --> 09:44.125
Please choose your opponent
and touch them.

09:46.294 --> 09:48.588
Fuckin' zombies.

09:49.088 --> 09:51.090
Let's shoot them all!

09:51.173 --> 09:53.009
Get up!

10:04.770 --> 10:06.856
Please play your cards.

10:34.300 --> 10:35.343
Nobu.

10:37.678 --> 10:39.013
You're a zombie, aren't you?

10:40.306 --> 10:41.182
Huh?

10:42.391 --> 10:43.559
I can tell.

10:45.811 --> 10:46.729
Listen.

10:47.229 --> 10:49.482
I need you to do exactly what I say.

10:53.611 --> 10:55.404
It's too bad, you know?

10:55.488 --> 10:57.615
I really thought
you'd have figured it out by now.

10:57.698 --> 11:00.493
How far the infection has
actually spread out there.

11:00.993 --> 11:04.705
From where I'm sitting, you might be
better off as a zombie after all.

11:05.206 --> 11:06.582
What?

11:07.333 --> 11:09.043
How could you possibly know that?

11:10.586 --> 11:13.631
Because I know that humans
are emotional creatures.

11:13.714 --> 11:16.175
It takes a lot to shoot someone.

11:16.676 --> 11:18.803
And those Vaccine cards are so precious.

11:18.886 --> 11:21.389
You think they'd just
use one on a stranger?

11:22.014 --> 11:25.101
And while the little humans
hold on to their cards,

11:25.184 --> 11:27.937
the zombies will multiply and multiply.

11:28.813 --> 11:30.564
And once you're infected,

11:30.648 --> 11:34.527
there'd be no reason to hold off
on using your Zombie card to win.

11:35.695 --> 11:39.990
When the game started,
there were four zombies.

11:40.074 --> 11:42.743
If the infection were
to grow exponentially,

11:42.827 --> 11:45.162
which is what
math would tell us to expect,

11:45.246 --> 11:49.166
to go from four zombies to a majority
of the players would take

11:50.167 --> 11:52.002
three rounds.

11:54.630 --> 11:57.508
Isn't it obvious
which side has the advantage?

11:59.927 --> 12:01.846
Mmm, not fallin' for that.

12:02.847 --> 12:04.348
Why would I believe ya?

12:04.432 --> 12:07.643
Whether you believe me or not is
completely besides the point.

12:07.727 --> 12:10.146
Either you're gonna shoot me and I'll die,

12:10.229 --> 12:13.315
which gives you
a couple more rounds before you're killed,

12:14.108 --> 12:16.610
or you accept my deal now.

12:17.111 --> 12:19.905
You become a zombie, and you survive.

12:42.845 --> 12:44.722
Show your cards.

13:04.784 --> 13:06.786
It's tempting.

13:06.869 --> 13:08.996
But I'm gonna pass on your deal.

13:30.643 --> 13:31.685
No.

13:31.769 --> 13:33.062
Masato…

13:34.188 --> 13:36.649
- We're too late.
- We're not gonna make it.

13:37.233 --> 13:38.317
Rei'll be next.

13:38.400 --> 13:40.444
- We're finished!
- Nobu.

13:40.528 --> 13:41.821
- We're gonna die!
- Nobu!

13:43.656 --> 13:45.157
Remember what I told you.

14:00.631 --> 14:02.842
We're in charge. We're gonna win.

14:03.801 --> 14:05.261
At what cost?

14:06.470 --> 14:08.055
This has gone too far!

14:08.556 --> 14:12.393
The zombies want to kill us
because we killed their teammates.

14:12.476 --> 14:13.811
But we don't have to be scared.

14:14.603 --> 14:18.190
You know zombies don't have a way
to kill humans in this game.

14:19.316 --> 14:22.820
Although if you do wanna die,
you can get infected any time you want.

14:26.532 --> 14:29.660
Those guys are losing it.
We gotta get out of here.

14:33.080 --> 14:34.540
Nobu! Hey, Nobu!

14:34.623 --> 14:37.042
Hurry! Stay down!

14:40.713 --> 14:41.589
What's going on?

14:41.672 --> 14:43.549
You gotta listen to me.

14:55.728 --> 14:56.937
What's wrong?

15:04.904 --> 15:06.363
Bitch tricked us.

15:32.389 --> 15:33.724
Rei…

15:41.774 --> 15:43.067
You're not dead.

15:46.820 --> 15:48.697
Two rounds remain.

15:48.781 --> 15:52.076
- Choose your opponent and touch them.
- We gotta find them!

15:54.912 --> 15:56.914
Why did you pick me to play against?

15:58.958 --> 16:01.377
Rei, I wanna know
who you think is gonna win.

16:06.715 --> 16:08.384
The zombies, obviously.

16:10.427 --> 16:13.555
- And that's what you've always believed?
- Well, yeah.

16:14.056 --> 16:17.726
Either the zombies win because they grow
exponentially, which would make sense,

16:17.810 --> 16:21.563
or the humans become merciless killers
and execute all the zombies.

16:22.106 --> 16:24.650
I figured it would come down
to one or the other.

16:26.485 --> 16:28.821
- Rei.
- Arisu?

16:29.488 --> 16:30.864
Be honest with me.

16:31.907 --> 16:33.534
You're not a zombie, are you?

16:35.077 --> 16:37.371
Please play your cards.

16:42.668 --> 16:44.670
Let's suppose you are a zombie.

16:45.212 --> 16:48.048
You work hard to build
this trust barricade.

16:48.549 --> 16:50.926
And then what? What's your plan?

16:51.635 --> 16:54.972
If nobody opts to save you
with their vaccine, that means

16:55.472 --> 16:57.182
you'd be killed by the game.

16:59.059 --> 17:01.937
You wouldn't rely on someone
saving you out of gratitude.

17:03.439 --> 17:07.693
A calculating mind like yours?
No way that's a part of your plan.

17:07.776 --> 17:10.446
You might believe in humanity,
but you don't trust it.

17:11.321 --> 17:13.365
I see. Keep going, Arisu.

17:14.074 --> 17:18.662
Okay… Let's assume the zombie
thing was always just an act.

17:19.621 --> 17:21.749
Your plan makes a lot more sense.

17:22.750 --> 17:24.835
You think I'm that smart, Arisu?

17:26.253 --> 17:29.339
Even if you weren't a zombie at any point,
it still helps you.

17:29.840 --> 17:32.301
Because if you build trust
with a large enough group,

17:32.384 --> 17:34.261
if they buy into your logic,

17:34.845 --> 17:36.764
survival is guaranteed.

17:38.599 --> 17:42.603
So you lie,
and trust is born out of the lie.

17:43.645 --> 17:47.483
The illusion was the key.
That's how you survived.

17:50.694 --> 17:53.155
I see. That's a fascinating theory…

17:53.238 --> 17:56.325
And that's also why,
when you played against Ikeno last round,

17:56.408 --> 17:57.785
he didn't kill you.

17:59.328 --> 18:01.705
Because he still had
his Shotgun card, right?

18:02.414 --> 18:04.666
But because you're not a zombie,

18:04.750 --> 18:07.086
he would not have been
able to take you out.

18:08.837 --> 18:10.672
Show your cards.

18:20.057 --> 18:21.183
So?

18:22.184 --> 18:24.812
After all that,
you still didn't answer my question.

18:24.895 --> 18:26.188
Why play against me?

18:26.271 --> 18:28.816
I'm playing you to save you, Rei.

18:38.158 --> 18:39.159
A zombie?

18:45.332 --> 18:50.129
Even somebody who's that honorable
can still tell a lie.

18:56.135 --> 18:57.761
Now you're a zombie too.

18:58.762 --> 19:01.306
But if the zombies were
always going to win,

19:02.141 --> 19:03.642
why not become one right away?

19:04.852 --> 19:09.314
I thought about that for a long while,
but I couldn't commit too soon.

19:09.898 --> 19:13.902
The barricade wasn't a con. Back then,
I thought the humans had a chance.

19:13.986 --> 19:16.071
That's why I built it in the first place.

19:18.699 --> 19:20.576
But I couldn't really know.

19:21.076 --> 19:22.995
My plan was to make a choice
late in the game.

19:23.912 --> 19:27.666
But… after watching Ikeno and the others,

19:28.250 --> 19:30.878
I started to see that ruthlessness

19:32.045 --> 19:34.006
was just what the humans needed.

19:37.676 --> 19:39.011
But now I see.

19:39.720 --> 19:41.680
I know which side will win.

19:43.015 --> 19:44.224
So thank you.

19:45.225 --> 19:48.687
The final round will now begin.

19:49.730 --> 19:50.981
We gotta go.

19:52.399 --> 19:54.484
How long have you been a zombie, Arisu?

19:56.361 --> 19:57.321
I always was.

20:01.700 --> 20:03.202
Oh, he's good.

20:05.329 --> 20:06.371
Natsu!

20:08.540 --> 20:10.751
- Shion!
- Arisu!

20:14.838 --> 20:16.840
I got infected, just like Nobu said to do.

20:16.924 --> 20:19.009
Just one more round to make
sure we're all zombies.

20:20.719 --> 20:21.887
Where's Nobu now?

20:22.554 --> 20:23.805
He went to find Tetsu.

20:34.691 --> 20:35.943
Shit!

20:36.443 --> 20:37.653
Tetsu!

20:38.904 --> 20:39.738
Tetsu!

20:46.078 --> 20:46.954
Wait, please.

20:47.663 --> 20:49.206
Just wait, hang on a sec!

20:51.375 --> 20:52.793
- Ah.
- Get off of me!

20:55.420 --> 20:57.631
- Not here.
- What about down there?

20:57.714 --> 20:58.840
No, I checked!

21:00.509 --> 21:03.095
- Hey! He's over here!
- Come on! Let's go!

21:03.595 --> 21:05.514
Go, go! Get them!

21:19.403 --> 21:20.696
Get back here!

21:25.534 --> 21:28.912
- Run! We're out of time! Find Tetsu!
- Yeah! Okay!

21:33.834 --> 21:35.585
Tetsu!

21:43.510 --> 21:44.511
Over here!

21:46.263 --> 21:47.264
That way!

21:47.347 --> 21:49.516
Come on, quick! He's down there!

21:54.730 --> 21:57.983
Please choose your opponent
and touch them.

21:58.734 --> 22:00.152
Nobu! You have to do it now!

22:01.320 --> 22:04.072
You can't kill me without a shotgun!
Bring it on!

22:08.160 --> 22:09.745
Show your cards.

22:16.376 --> 22:17.919
Tetsu.

22:18.003 --> 22:20.047
Tetsu!

22:20.130 --> 22:22.382
I can explain it all later.

22:29.306 --> 22:31.099
No!

22:32.893 --> 22:34.478
It's okay, Kazuya.

22:36.229 --> 22:37.564
This is gonna save you.

22:39.941 --> 22:40.776
Huh?

22:42.361 --> 22:44.905
The final round is over.

22:47.532 --> 22:50.369
Now announcing totals.

22:52.371 --> 22:53.497
Zombies…

22:54.122 --> 22:55.540
Thirty-two.

22:56.833 --> 22:57.709
Humans…

22:59.294 --> 23:00.670
Thirteen.

23:01.880 --> 23:04.174
Zombies win.

23:09.930 --> 23:12.349
Oh, I can't believe it!

23:19.773 --> 23:24.945
With only 13 people,
it is game over for the humans.

23:32.327 --> 23:33.912
Fucking hell…

23:46.091 --> 23:49.469
- Yes! I can't believe it!
- We won!

24:32.804 --> 24:34.055
You should come with us.

25:05.921 --> 25:08.173
PLEASE PROCEED 16 KM SOUTHWEST

25:08.256 --> 25:11.426
THE "GAME" WILL BE HELD
AT SUNDOWN IN TWO DAYS

25:27.067 --> 25:28.693
You don't need to feel guilty.

25:35.450 --> 25:37.202
I'm not feeling anything.

25:38.870 --> 25:39.996
It's only a game.

25:41.831 --> 25:43.291
That's right.

25:47.504 --> 25:50.048
Let's get some sleep.

25:59.349 --> 26:01.393
And finished.

26:01.476 --> 26:03.895
Doing this will help
with the morning tangles.

26:04.396 --> 26:06.398
Thank you, big sis.

26:06.481 --> 26:08.984
I'm not your sis.

26:16.241 --> 26:17.075
Hey, look.

26:18.326 --> 26:20.161
Isn't Arisu gonna sleep?

26:23.123 --> 26:25.625
He's probably thinking about his wife.

26:27.294 --> 26:28.670
Yeah.

26:28.753 --> 26:30.589
I wish mine were like that.

26:31.548 --> 26:33.383
My husband would never.

26:33.466 --> 26:35.302
Too busy getting angry.

26:35.385 --> 26:37.053
Too busy hitting me.

26:38.471 --> 26:41.224
Every day, I woke up wishing he was dead.

26:43.643 --> 26:47.063
But that sort of devotion…
it must be really nice.

26:52.777 --> 26:53.987
You bitch!

26:54.070 --> 26:56.239
- You're worthless! Fuck you!
- No, please! Stop!

28:00.970 --> 28:03.348
- Arisu…
- Will I see you tonight?

28:05.934 --> 28:07.519
Hey, Usagi.

28:08.269 --> 28:09.479
Where are you?

28:14.442 --> 28:15.735
Arisu…

28:17.320 --> 28:18.196
Hmm?

28:20.031 --> 28:21.282
I'll come get you.

28:37.632 --> 28:38.675
Usagi?

28:39.801 --> 28:40.677
Please.

28:40.760 --> 28:42.053
Wait, hold on--

28:42.721 --> 28:45.473
Dad… I'm sorry.

28:47.142 --> 28:48.518
When I dream…

28:50.228 --> 28:51.730
I can feel him.

28:52.355 --> 28:54.274
My father's presence.

28:57.610 --> 28:59.237
I wanna see him again.

29:00.947 --> 29:03.199
And even if he dies in the dream…

29:04.492 --> 29:06.536
I want to feel that pain again.

29:12.125 --> 29:13.960
Daddy. Don't leave.

29:14.544 --> 29:16.963
Dad! Please, no! Don't do it!

29:17.046 --> 29:19.007
Don't do it!

29:26.181 --> 29:28.683
There's something
I wanna ask you about your father.

29:31.478 --> 29:32.353
Can you help me?

29:35.190 --> 29:38.026
If my father is in my dreams…

29:39.778 --> 29:41.905
then I need to be where I can find him.

29:44.449 --> 29:45.909
Even in a nightmare.

30:29.118 --> 30:30.578
Hey, look out.

31:15.415 --> 31:16.833
Get down!

31:18.376 --> 31:20.503
Stop using these people as shields!

31:20.587 --> 31:22.422
You should be looking out for yourself.

31:34.017 --> 31:35.435
Whoa! Move!

32:02.962 --> 32:04.672
Come on!

32:14.182 --> 32:16.809
- Ryuji, when I move, you go.
- Uh-huh.

32:43.211 --> 32:46.047
I still can't believe
you made it through with the wheelchair.

32:46.965 --> 32:49.884
Yeah, well… I had a bit of help.

32:50.593 --> 32:52.929
Usagi, are you, like, a pro athlete?

32:53.554 --> 32:54.555
Nope.

32:55.556 --> 32:57.600
I do climb mountains as a hobby, though.

32:59.060 --> 33:01.813
It's like I've…
met you before or something.

33:03.982 --> 33:08.236
Hang on. Usagi's, like,
your real name, not a nickname?

33:08.319 --> 33:10.613
- Usagi…
- Yep.

33:12.490 --> 33:14.450
Your dad was
a mountain climber, too, right?

33:15.868 --> 33:18.913
Maybe I saw your name
in a sports magazine.

33:18.997 --> 33:21.958
Wait, no. You mean
the guy who was all over the news?

33:22.041 --> 33:24.377
Because he killed himself
after he lied about a climb?

33:24.460 --> 33:26.337
Yeah, him.

33:27.213 --> 33:28.131
Oh…

33:28.840 --> 33:29.841
My bad.

33:31.259 --> 33:34.429
Those magazines are trashy.
I wouldn't worry about 'em.

33:35.763 --> 33:37.932
- Hey.
- Trashy but true.

33:38.016 --> 33:40.184
You think the suicide thing is true too?

33:40.268 --> 33:42.687
- Why don't you ask her?
- No way! I can't.

33:42.770 --> 33:43.771
Ask her.

33:43.855 --> 33:45.857
You don't really care
what they think, right?

33:47.650 --> 33:50.820
My dad wasn't the kind of person
who would lie to anyone.

33:52.739 --> 33:54.240
He wouldn't kill himself, either.

33:57.869 --> 33:59.787
You probably have
to tell people that every day.

33:59.871 --> 34:02.040
But, be honest, do you really believe it?

34:03.875 --> 34:05.418
If it weren't for you,

34:06.753 --> 34:08.546
I would never have come back here.

34:09.797 --> 34:10.757
Really?

34:11.549 --> 34:14.844
It's funny. When we first met,
I felt like we were the same.

34:16.137 --> 34:19.057
That we were both consumed
by thoughts of death.

34:21.893 --> 34:24.312
You wanted to be with your dead father.

34:25.688 --> 34:28.816
Right? That's what you've always wanted
more than anything.

34:30.026 --> 34:33.196
You would never have accepted
my invitation otherwise.

34:34.655 --> 34:37.450
You're not wrong,
but I never wanted to come back here.

34:40.286 --> 34:42.080
I didn't want to make Arisu suffer.

34:42.163 --> 34:44.290
Deep down, you don't believe that.

34:44.373 --> 34:46.334
No. That's not who I am.

34:49.045 --> 34:52.131
I've always wanted to come here.
To see it.

34:52.215 --> 34:54.258
I couldn't stop thinking about it.

34:54.342 --> 34:56.803
This in-between place linking our world

34:57.428 --> 34:58.888
to the land of death.

35:16.239 --> 35:18.407
I knew you'd be the one to survive.

35:20.368 --> 35:21.828
Who are you?

35:23.955 --> 35:25.164
Tell me.

35:26.624 --> 35:28.084
Do you know who I am?

35:29.252 --> 35:30.128
Oh yes.

35:30.878 --> 35:34.549
I've devoted my new life
to finding people just like you.

35:35.383 --> 35:38.928
People with the right qualities
to become capable citizens.

35:40.138 --> 35:41.013
What do you mean?

35:43.641 --> 35:46.227
You've played these games
many times before.

35:46.727 --> 35:50.231
Despite your condition,
you fought your way through, and survived.

35:50.314 --> 35:51.983
You reached your goal.

35:53.693 --> 35:55.486
You should remember now.

36:01.701 --> 36:03.578
I have a request for you.

36:04.287 --> 36:07.540
There's a certain woman
I want you to bring to this place.

36:08.332 --> 36:12.336
And in exchange, I will make sure
you see the world you desire.

36:13.963 --> 36:16.841
Am I right that you want
to see the land of death?

36:17.925 --> 36:20.553
For far beyond this place between worlds,

36:20.636 --> 36:23.055
you will find death's true domain.

36:25.433 --> 36:26.767
So what will it be?

36:26.851 --> 36:28.769
Do you agree to my terms?

36:30.396 --> 36:34.775
If I do this,
promise me I'll get what I want.

36:35.443 --> 36:37.653
- You will.
- How do I get her here?

36:38.779 --> 36:41.407
This woman still carries within her heart

36:41.490 --> 36:43.618
the shadow of her dead father.

36:45.494 --> 36:48.623
Invite her to this place,
and she will come.

36:49.207 --> 36:50.583
What do you mean?

36:51.334 --> 36:52.710
How do I invite her?

36:56.672 --> 36:58.382
Just have her drink this.

37:00.509 --> 37:03.638
You do that,
and you'll get what you've always wanted.

37:05.431 --> 37:07.683
So… are you in?

37:20.571 --> 37:21.656
All right.

37:24.200 --> 37:25.868
I'll do it.

37:43.469 --> 37:44.762
I have to admit,

37:45.263 --> 37:47.932
I didn't think he would agree
to bring her here.

37:50.268 --> 37:54.063
But your plan is coming together.
And Arisu has joined as well.

37:56.357 --> 37:58.567
Arisu won't abandon Usagi.

37:59.527 --> 38:03.823
I've learned that human emotions are like…
invisible threads.

38:03.906 --> 38:06.450
One only has to pull to make them move.

38:08.286 --> 38:10.037
So what's your next step?

38:11.330 --> 38:15.459
To put Ryuji to good use.
The man is quite an asset.

38:17.545 --> 38:19.839
An asset, maybe, but odd too.

38:20.548 --> 38:22.925
Who goes looking for the land of death?

38:23.009 --> 38:25.011
He's far from normal, to be sure.

38:25.094 --> 38:28.014
But he and Usagi are connected
in spirit now.

38:28.848 --> 38:31.809
Those threads get pulled, and he's mine.

38:33.477 --> 38:36.397
The game is finally getting interesting.

38:41.819 --> 38:43.070
Wonderful idea.

38:44.071 --> 38:45.156
Hmm.

39:07.011 --> 39:10.389
The required number
of teams has been reached.

39:11.807 --> 39:14.268
The game will now begin.

39:16.270 --> 39:19.940
THE TRAIN IS ARRIVING

40:17.873 --> 40:21.043
NOT IN SERVICE

40:27.258 --> 40:30.219
Game, Runaway Train.

40:43.190 --> 40:48.612
Game rules.
This train is operated without a driver.

40:48.696 --> 40:53.534
If you can successfully move from
the starting car to the lead car,

40:53.617 --> 40:55.119
and, after hearing the siren…

40:56.287 --> 40:59.457
…stop the train, you clear the game.

41:01.041 --> 41:05.463
When you move to the next car,
the door will automatically lock.

41:05.546 --> 41:07.089
And after 30 seconds,

41:07.173 --> 41:10.926
either oxygen or poison gas
will be released.

41:11.594 --> 41:12.720
Poison gas?

41:12.803 --> 41:14.597
Excluding this starting car,

41:14.680 --> 41:17.057
you will proceed through eight train cars.

41:17.141 --> 41:20.269
Poison gas will be released
in four of the cars.

41:20.853 --> 41:22.646
Upon entering a new car,

41:22.730 --> 41:26.984
you will have 30 seconds to decide
whether to put on your mask.

41:27.067 --> 41:30.654
Each player will receive five canisters.

41:31.155 --> 41:32.531
Please attach the canister

41:32.615 --> 41:35.576
to the insertion port
on the right side of your mask.

41:36.619 --> 41:41.624
Inside these canisters is
a neutralizing agent for the poison gas.

41:42.875 --> 41:46.462
You cannot use other players' canisters.

41:47.713 --> 41:52.092
Additionally,
you cannot return to previous cars.

41:54.345 --> 41:57.723
Please secure the canisters to your arm

41:57.806 --> 42:00.059
and collect your gas mask.

42:13.447 --> 42:15.241
Game start.

42:15.324 --> 42:18.327
Please proceed to the next car.

42:47.231 --> 42:48.732
Why is there a bird?

42:50.943 --> 42:54.029
The canary acts as a warning.
Just like in a coal mine.

42:55.155 --> 42:56.699
If it dies, it's poison.

42:57.866 --> 42:59.034
Okay.

43:01.161 --> 43:03.497
Please make your choice.

43:42.536 --> 43:43.579
What do we do?

43:48.459 --> 43:49.793
Sohta…

44:03.807 --> 44:05.893
It's not poison.

44:06.894 --> 44:10.439
Wait. Does that mean we wasted a canister?

44:11.023 --> 44:13.025
No, no. It's okay.

44:13.525 --> 44:17.488
There are still four cars with poison.
And we still have four canisters.

44:30.834 --> 44:33.504
Please proceed to the next car.

44:44.556 --> 44:47.893
Please make your choice.

45:27.766 --> 45:29.476
Oh my God!

45:32.646 --> 45:33.772
It was poison!

45:34.773 --> 45:36.358
It was and we're okay!

45:45.033 --> 45:46.452
CAR 3

45:48.537 --> 45:50.956
Please make your choice.

45:53.459 --> 45:54.752
So? What do we do?

45:58.255 --> 45:59.757
I'm not putting it on.

45:59.840 --> 46:00.883
Why not?

46:01.550 --> 46:02.926
Because they know we're afraid.

46:03.010 --> 46:05.304
The game is betting
we'll use our masks early.

46:05.846 --> 46:08.348
They probably want us
to waste all our canisters.

46:08.432 --> 46:11.018
Then later… we get poisoned.

46:14.521 --> 46:17.941
- I'm not gonna use it for this car.
- That's still just basically chance.

46:18.567 --> 46:20.235
There must be a trick we're missing.

46:21.111 --> 46:24.156
This is the third car.
We still need to get through five more.

46:24.239 --> 46:28.160
We still have three more canisters
and three more poison gas cars.

46:30.746 --> 46:32.456
What should we do?

46:36.084 --> 46:37.419
No masks this time.

46:39.379 --> 46:41.298
What if your brother got it wrong, though?

46:41.381 --> 46:44.051
- Hey. What's your problem?
- You need to back the hell off.

47:24.842 --> 47:26.969
No matter what you do,
you can't survive the gas.

47:39.857 --> 47:42.734
It's not poison! We're okay!

47:48.532 --> 47:49.825
We can make it.

47:49.908 --> 47:51.410
She saved us.

48:17.561 --> 48:19.813
It's heading toward Asakusa!

48:20.397 --> 48:23.775
I know that line! I'm pretty sure
it's heading west to Omotesando!

48:23.859 --> 48:24.735
You're a train nerd?

49:05.108 --> 49:07.986
If we put our masks on
but it's not a poison car,

49:08.570 --> 49:10.530
we won't have enough left to make it.

49:13.033 --> 49:15.953
You. You know a lot about trains?

49:17.996 --> 49:21.124
- Yeah.
- Those people on the other train.

49:21.208 --> 49:23.585
It looked like it took a while
for them to die.

49:23.669 --> 49:26.254
They must be using a gas
that's heavier than air.

49:26.755 --> 49:29.716
They'd need a massive amount
to fill up a whole train car.

49:29.800 --> 49:33.011
- So what?
- So there'd need to be a tank for the gas.

49:33.512 --> 49:36.390
Any car with poison would need space
to house a tank that big.

49:36.473 --> 49:37.474
Where would it be?

49:38.141 --> 49:40.143
No, no. I have no idea. I don't know!

49:40.227 --> 49:43.063
Hey! We're running out of time!
What do we choose?

49:44.356 --> 49:46.274
What if that other train was a trick?

49:47.651 --> 49:51.655
What if maybe they showed us that
on purpose, to try and scare us?

49:51.738 --> 49:52.990
Yeah, maybe.

49:53.073 --> 49:56.785
If we use our masks now,
we might not have enough for the rest.

49:58.578 --> 49:59.454
Wait…

50:03.583 --> 50:08.088
I'm not sure,
but… this type of… of train car…

50:08.588 --> 50:10.716
It probably shouldn't have a pantograph.

50:11.299 --> 50:12.592
What's a pantograph?

50:13.427 --> 50:14.553
The thing on the roof?

50:14.636 --> 50:16.013
Exactly.

50:16.096 --> 50:18.598
It's the thing that draws
electricity for the train.

50:18.682 --> 50:20.976
Because if it has one, it really takes up…

50:21.059 --> 50:23.437
It takes up a lot of room
on the train's roof.

50:23.979 --> 50:28.400
This car… shouldn't have one.
So the roof would be open.

50:29.526 --> 50:33.655
Let me get this straight.
There's space up there for a gas tank?

50:36.867 --> 50:38.785
Yeah. Should be.

50:40.412 --> 50:41.955
Should be?

50:42.039 --> 50:43.832
Are we really gonna trust this guy?

50:46.043 --> 50:47.753
Please make your choice.

50:53.383 --> 50:55.469
- What do we do?
- I don't know!

52:14.214 --> 52:15.966
Let me out!

52:18.260 --> 52:21.012
- I'm so sorry!
- Yuna! Get away! Move away!

52:33.733 --> 52:34.860
Help…

53:04.556 --> 53:06.850
CAR 5

53:14.274 --> 53:16.651
There are four cars left,
including this one.

53:16.735 --> 53:19.446
We only have two oxygen canisters left,
then we're out.

53:19.529 --> 53:22.073
And we know there are still
two cars with poison gas.

53:23.033 --> 53:24.034
What's this one?

53:26.411 --> 53:27.579
This particular car

53:28.580 --> 53:30.624
would have a pantograph on the roof.

53:31.291 --> 53:34.502
So then… there's no room for a gas tank.

54:22.884 --> 54:25.971
CAR 6

54:28.098 --> 54:29.099
Wait…

54:31.643 --> 54:33.603
The luggage racks are different.

54:35.397 --> 54:37.274
- Oh no.
- What is it?

54:39.901 --> 54:41.027
I was wrong.

54:41.111 --> 54:42.904
I got the model of the train wrong.

54:42.988 --> 54:44.197
What?

54:44.281 --> 54:47.575
Uh, I'm sorry, but it's not
the type that I thought it was.

54:47.659 --> 54:51.246
So the… positions
of the pantographs are different.

54:52.831 --> 54:55.709
I'm sorry! I have no idea what to do!

54:58.378 --> 55:00.171
So up to this point, it's all been luck?

55:01.881 --> 55:03.717
- Yeah.
- You could have got us killed!

55:03.800 --> 55:04.801
You piece of shit!

55:04.884 --> 55:06.928
- You're supposed to be a train nerd!
- Ow!

55:07.012 --> 55:09.180
Stop it!

55:09.264 --> 55:10.473
We're out of time.

55:12.392 --> 55:14.853
Please make your choice.

55:16.313 --> 55:20.317
Two oxygen canisters left,
and two gas cars left.

55:20.817 --> 55:22.861
We can't afford any more mistakes.

55:36.833 --> 55:38.251
So we just go with our gut?

55:40.503 --> 55:41.463
Mmm.

55:48.470 --> 55:51.890
I'm with you. I'm trusting her gut.

55:56.519 --> 55:57.604
Me too.

55:58.980 --> 56:00.482
I'm betting on Usagi.

56:01.399 --> 56:02.734
I've got a good feeling.

56:08.365 --> 56:09.991
Sure, let's take a chance.

56:13.995 --> 56:15.872
In the end, it's a game of luck.

56:32.389 --> 56:34.682
Be poison gas.
Be poison gas. Be poison gas.

56:34.766 --> 56:37.143
Be poison gas.
Be poison gas. Be poison gas!

56:59.707 --> 57:00.708
It's alive.

57:01.459 --> 57:03.086
This isn't poison!
